   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Elan beats Mr. Halvorsen twice in the park and gets bored with the games under the sycamore.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Elan studies with Mr. Halvorsen all summer and wins the state tournament as a result.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"A highly rated young player beats an older park player, is challenged to understand his moves, studies with him, and later handles an unfamiliar position calmly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"An arrogant teenager finally learns his lesson and becomes a much better person.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A highly rated young player beats an older park player, is challenged to understand his moves, studies with him, and later handles an unfamiliar position calmly.$q$, $q$The correct choice traces the whole arc without judging Elan. The passage says he drew one game at the state tournament; it never says he won the tournament.$q$, 'draft', '9aea529c-f612-53d7-9bc0-132ec2e4b363')
